.\" Distro-authored man page for the Fedora pidp8i package.
.\" Candidate for upstreaming to the PiDP-8/I project.
.TH PIDP8I-SIM 1 "November 21, 2026" "PiDP-8/I" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pidp8i-sim \- PDP-8 simulator with PiDP-8 front-panel emulation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pidp8i-sim
.br
.B pidp8i-sim-nls
.br
.B pidp8i-sim-ils
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pidp8i-sim
is the SIMH PDP-8 engine built for the PiDP-8/I cabinet: it drives the
physical or simulated front panel (lamps, switches, pulse and run
buttons) over the Raspberry Pi GPIO, and boots scripts from
.IR /usr/share/pidp8i/boot
when the panel's boot-selector switches say so.
.PP
On a machine without GPIO panel hardware it refuses to run:
it prints
.I "No GPIO chips found"
and exits 1. Start the simulator through
.BR pidp8i (1)
(the user service and its screen session) rather than directly, and use
.BR pdp8 (1)
when you just want the simulator console without a panel.
.PP
The two additional names are hard links to the same binary that force
a lamp mode instead of deciding from the build configuration:
.B pidp8i-sim-nls
runs with the incandescent lamp simulator disabled (NLS), and
.B pidp8i-sim-ils
forces the incandescent lamp simulator (ILS) that mimics the glow and
decay of the original bulbs on the panel LEDs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/share/pidp8i/boot/
boot scripts, selected by front-panel switch state
.TP
.B /var/lib/pidp8i/run/
PID file of the running session
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pidp8i (1),
.BR pdp8 (1),
.BR pidp8i-test (1),
.BR scanswitch (8),
the upstream README and
.I doc/configure-options.md
under
.IR /usr/share/doc/pidp8i/
